# Variant projector09220931 of boards/hy200-qz713df-a1: the "HY300 Pro+" (2025, DDR3), stock
# Android 11 of 2025-09-22. No unit of ours: the profile comes from the update.img in the firmware
# archive (installer profile, J); the run from its owner. Read after ../../board.env; a key here wins.
VARIANT=projector09220931
# Verified by its owner (issue #4, 30.10.2026): his own build of main 591d0d3 with the crust clock
# of TODO 5.29 patched in by hand, installed with --test-image; picture, sound, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth,
# the remote, the fan, the power key, off and on again. His dump's report (01.11.2026) names this
# firmware in every feature of the profile. Not measured there: standby (crust stays experimental),
# the HDMI input, HDCP. *Superseded:* "nobody has run our firmware on a unit with this firmware".
STATUS=verified
VERIFIED_BY="jo-- (issue #4), HY300 Pro+ 2025-09 unit, own build of main 591d0d3, 30.10.2026"
IMAGE_NAME=h713-hy200-qz713df-a1-projector09220931
# the clock of this firmware's boot0 (boot0_sdcard.fex), and cstenger's on his bench
DRAM_CLK=624
# FEATURES: none. The owner's unit (issue #4) has no focus motor, no headphone jack and no camera,
# although this firmware's stock tree drives a motor (motor_ctr okay, the HY310's step tables);
# the board's tree leaves it off, which is right for his unit. Accelerometer: not measured.
# the name in the network (TODO 5.18, the owner 11.10.2026: the name on the box)
HOSTNAME_BOARD=hy300proplus
